WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.102
Thanks again for being here
every time.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:05.371
I saw that your name tag said
"Tyler from New Orleans."

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.707
-New Orleans, yeah, born and
raised, New Orleans, man.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.642
-Is that right?
I thought it was Atlanta.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.345
-No, no, I went to Atlanta --
I moved to Atlanta in like '92.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.814
I was like 18, 19 years old.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.783
There's -- you know,
White kids go to the beach

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.951
for spring break.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.585
Black kids were
going to Atlanta.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:20.686
-Oh.
-Don't know why.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.021
There was no beach.
I don't know.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.624
We just went to Atlanta
for a thing called Freaknik.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.959
-Freaknik?

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.693
-Yeah, it's like a picnic for
freaks when you're young.

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:29.429
It was -- it was really cool.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.963
But while everybody's there
having a good time,

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:33.199
everybody's like,
you know, partying.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.634
You know what people
do on spring break.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.169
They're -- you know,
they're doing that.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.903
But I was seeing
Black people do well

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:38.938
for the first time in my life.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.973
I was shocked at how well
they were doing.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.409
So I went back to New Orleans
and loaded up my Hyundai

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.944
and moved to Atlanta.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.112
That's where it all
started for me.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.113
-That's wild.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.648
I mean, now,
Tyler Perry Studios,

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.650
you have the largest studio

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.951
in the United States,
in the country.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.319
-That's what they tell me, yeah,
that's what they tell me.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.787
-Yeah.

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.889
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:59.826
I mean, they film everything
there, all these projects --

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.994
"Walking Dead,"
you did "Coming 2 America,"

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.829
"Red Notice," Marvel movies.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:05.064
-Marvel movies going on there,
yeah.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.332
-Do you know secrets?
Marvel secrets?

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.633
-I do not.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.502
Listen to me,
just to make this clear --

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.003
[ Drum beast ]

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:12.338
Come on, man,
there's no drum roll here!

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.505
No, no, no, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:19.278
I don't -- I don't go to --
like -- okay.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.582
When the stages are empty,
you know, something is going on,

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.017
I will go and make sure
everything

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.384
is all right at the stage.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:28.021
So if you see people rehearsing
and shooting things,

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.155
it's like, "Oh, wow,
that's cool.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.723
That's what's going
to be in the movie?"

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.058
And so you start
writing it down.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.058
But no,
that's not what I'm doing.

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:35.160
That's all B.S.
No.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.662
The only time I know
something is like

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.697
they'll call me up and they say
we're doing gunfire

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:40.833
or explosions or something like
that, they'll let me know.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.268
-Because you own the -- yeah
-Yeah.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.003
-So you can tell --
you would know

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.272
if Tobey Maguire
is in the new Spider-Man?

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.875
-I absolutely would, and I would
know all of those things,

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.509
because he would be there.
-Yeah, so you walk by,

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:51.877
he'll say, "Hey, Tyler,"
and you go, "Hey, Tobey."

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:53.613
-Yeah, I'm like, "I don't see
you. I don't see you."

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.880
-So you did -- you did see him?

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.282
-No, did not -- come on.
[ Drum beat ]

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.550
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.550 --> 00:01:59.919
That's good.
-Not bad, right?

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.154
-That's really good.
That's really good.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.254
Good work, good work.
-I'm telling you, man,

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.289
I'm working on my acting.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.724
I'm taking acting classes
on weekends.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:07.359
-That works, but just that whole
jolly, thing, man, that was --

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:09.262
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.429
-That was the worst.
-That was B.S.

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.098
-That was the worst move
I could ever do.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.165
I know.
-Won't let it go.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.299
-Will you never --
will you forget --

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:15.801
ever forget that I said "jolly?"

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.736
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.736 --> 00:02:19.772
You have ruined my entire
Christmas because every time

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.274
I see Santa,
I'm gonna think "jolly."

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.642
We lost because of that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:25.978
-I -- did you ever think that
you'd have this studio

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:28.280
and be open to so many different
projects and things

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.882
happening and that creative?

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.284
-It's a wonderful thing, no, no.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:34.620
All I wanted to do was --
was just -- I built the stages

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.122
so that everybody else could
rent them and use them,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.957
because i don't use the stages,
but I use the rest of the lot.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.225
-Yeah.
-So it's really great to see

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.893
all of these other productions
coming and setting

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.628
up shop and doing all these
great things.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:43.829
It's wonderful, man.
I love it.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.464
-We just talked about you
on the show.

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.599
We do -- I should send you a
text every time we talk,

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.068
but you get like crazy.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.503
But Whoopi Goldberg was here.
-Whoopi, I love Whoopi.

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:53.372
-Man, she was so funny,
she crushed,

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:54.674
and we were talking about
"Sister Act 3."

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.510
-Yeah, yeah.
-You made it happen.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.978
-I don't know if I made it
happen as much

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:02.882
as she made it happen,
but I wanted to be a part of it

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.751
to make sure that we
could get it done,

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.720
so I signed on to it so that we
could get it done, but yeah.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.154
She already laid the groundwork,
man.

00:03:09.154 --> 00:03:11.523
So to have "Sister Act 3" --
we need a "Sister Act."

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:12.925
Don't we need "Sister Act?"
I mean...

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.160
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.294
-I love it.
-Everything going on

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:16.729
in the country,
we need something good.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.832
We need some of that kind of
humor from back in the day.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.368
-Madea's back!
-Yes, yes, Madea's coming back.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.970
[ Laughs ]

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.404
I'll tell you, I was done, man.

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:27.339
I was done, but so much was
going on in the country,

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:28.674
I said, "You know,
we just need to laugh."

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.276
And what do I -- what tool

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.910
do I have in my box
that can make people laugh?

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.679
And it's Madea,
so I dusted her off.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.181
-Yeah.
-And here she comes.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.315
-And here she comes.
-Bigger and better

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.549
than ever, man.

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:39.118
-When does it come out?
Do we know?

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.353
-We don't have a date just yet,
but it's definitely on Netflix

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:43.222
and we're excited, so everybody
gets the chance to see it.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.558
-Yeah, and do you ever,
by the way, slip into Madea,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.926
like, just talking?

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.361
-Like I just did
a few minutes ago?

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.329
-Yes, exactly, but I'm saying,
like, in situations

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:52.165
where you shouldn't?
Where you're just like...

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.266
I don't know --
you what happens?

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.767
If I get excited,
my voice goes up high

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:58.170
and people think I'm trying to
do Madea, but I'm just excited.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.606
So I've been speaking
at funerals -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.741
-Oh, my, no, no, no, no, no.

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:04.810
-Yeah, and some of them
are on YouTube.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:08.747
I'm speaking at funerals,
and you hear my pitch go up

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:10.082
out of the excitement,
and people think

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:12.518
I'm making fun and doing
Madea, but that's my voice.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.787
She comes from me.
I own that broad!

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.555
[ Laughter ]
She comes from me.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.524
You hear that?
That's exactly right.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.591
-I own that broad.
-When we come back,

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:20.793
I want to talk about
your new movie...

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.161
"Don't Look Up."
-Yeah, "Don't Look Up."

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.163
-"Don't Look Up."
-"Don't Look Up." Tyler Perry.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.398
More right after the break.
Stick around, everyone.

